  ═══ HAS-A (inject + delegate) vs IS-A (extend) ═══

  interface FeeCalculator { BigDecimal calc(Txn t); }
  class StandardFeeCalculator  implements FeeCalculator { ... }
  class DiscountedFeeCalculator implements FeeCalculator { ... }

  // PREFER — COMPOSITION (loose coupling, runtime-swappable)
  class CompositionBasedService {
     private final FeeCalculator fees;        // HAS-A
     private final NotificationService notes; // HAS-A (multiple!)
     private final AuditLogger audit;         // HAS-A
     CompositionBasedService(FeeCalculator f, NotificationService n,
                             AuditLogger a){ fees=f; notes=n; audit=a; }
     void process(Txn t){ var fee = fees.calc(t); audit.log(t); notes.send(t);}
     // calc() NOT exposed — controlled, delegated API
  }

  // AVOID unless TRUE is-a / framework / Template Method
  class InheritanceBasedService extends StandardFeeCalculator { }
  //   single parent only, leaks calc() publicly, no runtime swap

  SOLID: DIP (depend on FeeCalculator abstraction) + OCP (add impls freely).
  Pattern: Strategy via constructor injection. Rule: when in doubt → COMPOSE.
```
